## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | docs/ci.md | ⚠️ important docs ci md contradicts the implemented lookup failure behavior docs ci md 266 states the artefact cache class is kept on any ticket state lookup failure never delete blind the implemented — and tested — behavior is narrower a lookup failure blocks only the early reclaim a stale 24h cache is still deleted by the 24h backstop bash scripts sweep stale drafts sh 241 245 elif stale true then gh api x delete repos repo releases id dev null everything else in the pr states the carve out this sentence is the outlier the script s own header sweep stale drafts sh 47 48 kept on any ticket state lookup failure never delete blind — only the 24h backstop then applies the pr description s own test coverage bullet 24h backstop for open unknown state the art backstop unknown stale test which asserts the delete fires and reasons it only blocks the early reclaim an auditor tracing a deleted state unknown cache would read docs ci md as a promise of keep — and conclude the sweeper misbehaved when in fact it did exactly what the header tests specify two prose strings repeat the same misstatement by describing the swept cohort as ticket still open when it also includes state unknown drafts scripts sweep stale drafts sh 244 — swept after 24h with the ticket still open parked leg … — fires for lookup failures too scripts sweep stale drafts sh 412 — swept after 24h when the ticket stays open fix one lap doc only two prose strings reword docs ci md 266 to kept on any ticket state lookup failure — only the 24h backstop then applies mirroring the script header and make both prose strings say with the ticket still open or its state unknown |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | test/release_hygiene_test_support.dart | 💡 suggestion the gh stub s permission model doesn t cover the new issues lookup the stub maps every api call to need contents test release hygiene test support dart 536 — pre existing line so the new per ticket cycle state lookup gh api repos repo issues num scripts sweep stale drafts sh 234 passes permission enforcement in tests even though in production it needs the issues scope the pr notes say the call is covered by the job s existing issues write grant and docs ci md s stub rationale review of 294 is explicitly a dropped grant fails ci instead of silently degrading — but for this call a dropped issues grant stays green the stub serves the fixture regardless of the granted scopes while production 403s every lookup state stays empty and the early reclaim dies silently the 24h backstop survives so nothing breaks loudly — the feature just stops working with no test signal mirror the 294 precedent this stub comment cites — refine the need case so api repos issues n requires issues bash case cmd 2 in run list run view run watch run rerun need actions issue label need issues release need contents esac gh api scope follows the resource path gh 236 lookup issues read cmd api case 2 in issues need issues need contents esac suggestion level the issues grant as a whole is still pinned indirectly — the auto close test issue close 403s without it — so nothing blocks merge here this just closes the residual silent degradation window on the new call |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

// gh-236 artefact-cache draft lifecycle coverage, split into its own suite
// to keep release_hygiene_test.dart below the whole-tree 2800-line loc
// ratchet (gh-2318 precedent).
//
// The machine loop (dmtools-agents factory: timerAutoCommitAndSave.js →
// releaseArtefacts.uploadRawFile → github_get_or_create_draft_release, tag
// template `ai-{ticketKey}`) writes every fa leg's session/output snapshots
// as assets of a per-ticket DRAFT release `ai-gh-<n>` / `ai-pr-<n>` in this
// repo, created with the ai-teammate token — User-typed, marker-less, no
// Actions run owns it. Those drafts are caches by design (never published),
// but the sweeper's only bucket for them was the generic gh-2287 `bot`
// bucket: swept after 24h AND counted as sweep findings, so normal
// machine-loop traffic perpetually re-filed the sweep issue (gh-2287 →
// gh-2318 → gh-236). The lifecycle the class was missing:
//
//   ticket cycle ENDED (issue/PR closed) → reclaim NOW, any age — not a
//       sweep finding (a closed cycle never resumes; the pack's restore is
//       non-fatal and recreates the cache on "first run");
//   ticket still open, draft >24h (parked leg) → 24h backstop sweep as
//       before — silently, not a finding;
//   ticket open + fresh → kept untouched (an in-flight leg may own it);
//   ticket state UNKNOWN (lookup fails) → fail-safe: no reclaim, only the
//       24h backstop;
//   HUMAN-authored ai-* drafts → never lifecycle-deleted (E1 holds);
//   machine-authored NON-artifact drafts (vX.Y.Z) → remain bot-bucket
//       findings (the guard must not swallow real train drafts).
import 'dart:convert';
import 'dart:io';

import 'package:test/test.dart';

import 'release_hygiene_test_support.dart';

void main() {
  group(
    'gh-236 — machine-loop artefact-cache drafts (ai-gh-*/ai-pr-*) have a lifecycle',
    () {
      final freshDate = DateTime.now()
          .toUtc()
          .subtract(const Duration(hours: 1))
          .toIso8601String()
          .substring(0, 19);
      const oldDate = '2020-01-01T00:00:00Z';

      Map<String, Object> artDraft(
        String tag,
        int id, {
        String created = oldDate,
        String author = 'ai-teammate',
      }) => {
        'tag_name': tag,
        'id': id,
        'draft': true,
        'created_at': created,
